# PROJECT TITLE

AI StockVision — Intelligent Stock Chart Analysis, Prediction & Risk Management Platform

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, AI/ML engineer, financial data engineer, UI/UX designer, database architect, and cybersecurity specialist.

Build a complete, production-structured, full-stack web application called **AI StockVision**, designed for educational stock-market chart analysis, AI-assisted price forecasting, technical indicator analysis, risk management, and stock-market learning.

The website must have a beautiful, clean, transparent, modern, responsive, and professional interface with advanced animations and interactive financial charts.

The application must include a fully functional frontend, backend, MongoDB database, real AI integrations, email verification, an AI stock chatbot, chart-image analysis, interactive prediction levels, PDF report generation, and a complete user authentication system.

### CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS

* Build a real, working application rather than a static UI demonstration.
* Do not use mock data, fake stock prices, fabricated predictions, sample transactions, or hardcoded dashboard statistics.
* Do not display invented AI-generated predictions as real market data.
* All stock prices, historical candles, user records, saved reports, and analysis history must come from real data sources or actual user uploads.
* If a data provider or AI service is unavailable, display a clear error or unavailable state.
* Never silently replace failed API responses with sample data.
* Use environment variables for all API keys, database credentials, email credentials, and secrets.
* Implement proper authentication, authorization, input validation, error handling, logging, and rate limiting.
* Make all buttons, forms, filters, charts, navigation links, and dashboard features functional.
* Do not leave core features as TODOs or unfinished placeholders.
* If external API credentials are required, implement the integration completely and provide clear setup instructions.

